Releasing version rse03a.  I changed my checks in the code a bit so
that this concept should be portable to other classes and situations.

For example, a wizard might cast an illusion to look like food
(species enemy) or a god (ally).  A tourist might defile the high
temple of a sentient race (enemy), or a knight might slay a great
hunter of the species (ally).  This isn't in the spoiler section since
I haven't coded any of it - my patch still only affects rangers.

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#rse

DETAILS SPOILER:

Allies are domestic, and can be tamed with food.  Tamed allies untame
more slowly in your absence.

Only rangers get to-hit, damage, and dodge bonuses against their
species enemy.  Only neutral rangers are punished for attacking their
species ally.  Only rangers have species ally and enemy assigned.  All
other effects occur for any role.

